<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-Handelsbanken H1 profit up 26 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Handelsbanken H1 profit up 26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Handelsbanken on Tuesday presented these figures for the first half of the year, ending on June 30.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  3,776 vs   3,004</p>
<p> Net interest income		     5,387 vs   4,555</p>
<p> Net Commission			    1,582 vs   1,419</p>
<p>Net income from financial</p>
<p> transactions				  233 vs     795</p>
<p> Loan losses				   234 vs     952</p>
<p> Total income				7,659 vs   7,019</p>
<p> Operating costs			   3,649 vs   3,063</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     4,010 vs   3,956</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	   9.5  vs    11.7</p>
<p> Return on equity (pct)		  20.5  vs    18.4</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)				12.38 vs     9.70</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuter poll found Handelsbanken's operating profit was expected to rise to 3.66 billion crowns while loan losses were expected to more than halve to 428 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
